  78:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c **** 
  79:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c **** /** Function to encode and send any supported Network Layer Message.
  80:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * The payload for the message is encoded from information in the iArgs[] array.
  81:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * The contents of iArgs are are, per message type:
  82:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * - NETWORK_MESSAGE_WHO_IS_ROUTER_TO_NETWORK: Single int for DNET requested
  83:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * - NETWORK_MESSAGE_I_AM_ROUTER_TO_NETWORK: Array of DNET(s) to send,
  84:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * 		terminated with -1
  85:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * - NETWORK_MESSAGE_REJECT_MESSAGE_TO_NETWORK: array of 2 ints,
  86:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *      first is reason, second is DNET of interest
  87:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * - NETWORK_MESSAGE_ROUTER_BUSY_TO_NETWORK: same as I-Am-Router msg
  88:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * - NETWORK_MESSAGE_ROUTER_AVAILABLE_TO_NETWORK: same as I-Am-Router msg
  89:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * - NETWORK_MESSAGE_INIT_RT_TABLE and NETWORK_MESSAGE_INIT_RT_TABLE_ACK:
  90:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *      Array of DNET(s) to process as "Ports", terminated with -1.  Each DNET
  91:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *      will be expanded to a BACNET_ROUTER_PORT (with simple defaults for
  92:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *      most fields) and encoded.
  93:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *
  94:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param network_message_type [in] The type of message to be sent.
  95:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param dst [in/out] If not NULL, contains the destination for the message.
  96:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param iArgs [in] An optional array of values whose meaning depends on
  97:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *                   the type of message.
  98:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @return Number of bytes sent, or <=0 if no message was sent.
  99:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  */
