 288:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c **** /** Send an Initialize Routing Table message, built from an optional DNET[]
 289:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * array.
 290:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * There are two cases here:
 291:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * 1) We are requesting a destination router's Routing Table.
 292:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *    In that case, DNET[] should just have one entry of -1 (no routing table
 293:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *    is sent).
 294:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * 2) We are sending out our Routing Table for some reason (normally bcast it).
 295:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @ingroup NMRC
 296:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *
 297:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param dst [in] If NULL, msg will be broadcast to the local BACnet network.
 298:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *                 Optionally may designate a particular router destination,
 299:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *                 especially when requesting a Routing Table.
 300:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param DNET_list [in] List of BACnet network numbers for which I am a router,
 301:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *                       terminated with -1.  Will be just -1 when we are
 302:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *                       requesting a routing table.
 303:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  */
